"{\"document_name\":{\"0\":\"Aventro Edge Sedan.md\",\"1\":\"Adaptive Cruise Control (ACC).md\",\"2\":\" Aventro Motors- How to Change a Tyre.md\",\"3\":\"Test Drive at Your Doorstep.md\",\"4\":\"Aventro Storm SUV.md\",\"5\":\"How to Open the Fuel Knob in Aventro Cars.md\",\"6\":\"Sell Your Car in 3 Easy Steps.md\",\"7\":\"Parts-4.md\",\"8\":\"Best Ways to Maintain Good Mileage.md\",\"9\":\"How to Handle Engine Wont Start Issue.md\",\"10\":\"Careers.md\",\"11\":\"Parts-5.md\",\"12\":\"loans.md\",\"13\":\"Aventro  Connectivity.md\",\"14\":\"Aventro Pulse Hatchback.md\",\"15\":\"Best Ways to Use Your headlamps.md\",\"16\":\"Instrument Cluster Warning Alerts.md\",\"17\":\"Aventro Spark Hatchback.md\",\"18\":\"Adjusting the Steering Wheel.md\",\"19\":\"Parta-1.md\",\"20\":\"Adjusting the Seat Positions.md\",\"21\":\"How to Open the Hood of an Aventro Vehicle.md\",\"22\":\"Faq part-1.md\",\"23\":\"Aventro Motors Variants & Pricing.md\",\"24\":\"Aventro Grand SUV.md\",\"25\":\"Do and Donts About 3rd Party.md\",\"26\":\"Aventro Service Center Locations.md\",\"27\":\"Aventro Aero.md\",\"28\":\"Traction Control.md\",\"29\":\"About Aventro Motors.md\",\"30\":\"Aventro Glory SUV.md\",\"31\":\"What is ABS.md\",\"32\":\"Aventro Prime Sedan.md\",\"33\":\"Best Ways to Use Your Car AC.md\",\"34\":\"Pre-Owned Certified Cars.md\",\"35\":\"Opening and Closing the Boot.md\",\"36\":\"Aventro Swift Sedan.md\",\"37\":\"Discounts.md\",\"38\":\"Parts-6.md\",\"39\":\"How to Tow Your Aventro Car.md\",\"40\":\"How to Start Your Aventro Car.md\",\"41\":\"Safe Driving Checklist.md\",\"42\":\"Parts-2.md\",\"43\":\"Advice for Pregnant Women While in a Car.md\",\"44\":\" AventroZoom SUV.md\",\"45\":\"How to Open the Door When the Car Key Remote Battery is Dead.md\",\"46\":\"Parts-3.md\",\"47\":\"Lane Keeping Assist System.md\",\"48\":\"Aventro  Awards & Recognitions.md\",\"49\":\"Aventro Bolt Sedan.md\"},\"response\":{\"0\":null,\"1\":\"{\\n  \\\"items\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"category\\\": \\\"Specific Query\\\",\\n      \\\"query_text\\\": \\\"What exactly is Adaptive Cruise Control and how does it work in terms of detecting vehicles on the road?\\\",\\n      \\\"facts\\\": [\\n        \\\"Adaptive Cruise Control (ACC) is an advanced driver assistance system (ADAS) designed to automatically adjust a vehicle\\u2019s cruising speed to maintain a safe following distance from vehicles ahead.\\\",\\n        \\\"Adaptive Cruise Control: Uses sensors to detect vehicles ahead and can increase, decrease, or maintain speed based on traffic conditions.\\\",\\n        \\\"Constantly monitors the distance to the vehicle in front and adjusts speed to maintain a safe, pre-set gap.\\\"\\n      ],\\n      \\\"expected_answer\\\": \\\"Adaptive Cruise Control (ACC) is an advanced driver assistance system (ADAS) that uses sensors to detect vehicles ahead, automatically adjusting the vehicle\\u2019s speed to maintain a safe, pre-set gap.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"category\\\": \\\"Compound Query\\\",\\n      \\\"query_text\\\": \\\"How does ACC adjust speed when there's slower traffic ahead and what are the main components of the system, including the types of sensors used?\\\",\\n      \\\"facts\\\": [\\n        \\\"If a slower vehicle is detected within the pre-set following distance, ACC automatically reduces vehicle speed by controlling throttle and brakes.\\\",\\n        \\\"The system continuously scans the road ahead using radar, lidar, and\\/or cameras.\\\",\\n        \\\"Radar Sensors: Typically mounted in the grille or front bumper to detect vehicles ahead and measure their speed and distance.\\\",\\n        \\\"Lidar Sensors or Cameras: Used in some systems for enhanced object detection and lane tracking.\\\",\\n        \\\"ECU (Electronic Control Unit): Processes sensor data and commands the throttle and brakes as needed.\\\"\\n      ],\\n      \\\"expected_answer\\\": \\\"ACC adjusts speed by detecting slower vehicles ahead and automatically reducing speed through throttle and brake control. Its main components include radar sensors, lidar sensors or cameras, and an ECU.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"category\\\": \\\"Instructional Query\\\",\\n      \\\"query_text\\\": \\\"Can you provide step-by-step instructions on how to activate and use Adaptive Cruise Control in my vehicle?\\\",\\n      \\\"facts\\\": [\\n        \\\"The driver activates ACC and sets a desired speed and following distance (often via steering wheel controls).\\\",\\n        \\\"If the road ahead is clear, ACC maintains the set speed.\\\",\\n        \\\"If a slower vehicle is detected within the pre-set following distance, ACC automatically reduces vehicle speed by controlling throttle and brakes.\\\",\\n        \\\"If the vehicle ahead speeds up, ACC accelerates (up to the set speed limit).\\\",\\n        \\\"The system accelerates back to the set speed once the lane ahead is clear.\\\"\\n      ],\\n      \\\"expected_answer\\\": \\\"To use Adaptive Cruise Control, first activate ACC and set your desired speed and following distance using your steering wheel controls. The system will maintain the set speed if the road is clear, reduce speed if a slower vehicle is detected, accelerate when the vehicle speeds up, and resume the set speed once the lane is clear.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"category\\\": \\\"Opinion-Based Query\\\",\\n      \\\"query_text\\\": \\\"In your opinion, is Adaptive Cruise Control worth using for long highway drives, and what benefits does it offer?\\\",\\n      \\\"facts\\\": [\\n        \\\"Safety: Reduces risk of rear-end collisions.\\\",\\n        \\\"Convenience: Less driver fatigue on long trips and in traffic jams.\\\",\\n        \\\"Efficiency: Optimized speed and braking can improve fuel economy.\\\",\\n        \\\"In heavy traffic, can bring the car to a complete stop and resume motion as traffic moves.\\\"\\n      ],\\n      \\\"expected_answer\\\": \\\"Adaptive Cruise Control is worth using for long highway drives because it enhances safety by reducing collision risks, offers convenience by lessening driver fatigue, and improves fuel efficiency through optimized speed and braking.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"category\\\": \\\"Error\\/Issue Query\\\",\\n      \\\"query_text\\\": \\\"My car's Adaptive Cruise Control isn't decelerating when a slower vehicle is ahead. What could be causing this issue?\\\",\\n      \\\"facts\\\": [\\n        \\\"If a slower vehicle is detected within the pre-set following distance, ACC automatically reduces vehicle speed by controlling throttle and brakes.\\\",\\n        \\\"Sensor Limitations: May be affected by weather conditions, dirt, or obstructions.\\\",\\n        \\\"Not a Substitute for Attention: The driver must remain alert and ready to take control at all times.\\\"\\n      ],\\n      \\\"expected_answer\\\": \\\"If ACC isn't decelerating when a slower vehicle is ahead, it could be due to sensor limitations such as weather, dirt, or obstructions. Please note that the driver must remain alert and ready to take control at all times.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"category\\\": \\\"Edge-Case & Error Handling Query\\\",\\n      \\\"query_text\\\": \\\"acc not wrkin properly rn, speed ain't adjusting\\\",\\n      \\\"facts\\\": [\\n        \\\"Constantly monitors the distance to the vehicle in front and adjusts speed to maintain a safe, pre-set gap.\\\",\\n        \\\"If a slower vehicle is detected within the pre-set following distance, ACC automatically reduces vehicle speed by controlling throttle and brakes.\\\"\\n      ],\\n      \\\"expected_answer\\\": \\\"Adaptive Cruise Control should automatically adjust the speed when a slower vehicle is detected and maintain a safe following gap.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"category\\\": \\\"Competitor Related Query\\\",\\n      \\\"query_text\\\": \\\"How does your Adaptive Cruise Control system compare to other brands and why is it designed to work this way?\\\",\\n      \\\"facts\\\": [\\n        \\\"Adaptive Cruise Control (ACC) is an advanced driver assistance system (ADAS) designed to automatically adjust a vehicle\\u2019s cruising speed to maintain a safe following distance from vehicles ahead.\\\",\\n        \\\"Adaptive Cruise Control: Uses sensors to detect vehicles ahead and can increase, decrease, or maintain speed based on traffic conditions.\\\",\\n        \\\"Keeps the car traveling at a set speed until it detects a slower-moving vehicle in its path.\\\",\\n        \\\"Constantly monitors the distance to the vehicle in front and adjusts speed to maintain a safe, pre-set gap.\\\",\\n        \\\"Decelerates when a slower vehicle is detected, and speeds back up to the original set speed when the lane clears.\\\"\\n      ],\\n      \\\"expected_answer\\\": \\\"Our Adaptive Cruise Control system is designed to automatically adjust vehicle speed by detecting slower vehicles and maintaining a safe following distance, ensuring it stays at a set speed until a slower vehicle is detected, which is a reliable approach to enhancing road safety.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"category\\\": \\\"Feedback Related Query\\\",\\n      \\\"query_text\\\": \\\"I found your explanation of Adaptive Cruise Control a bit confusing and hard to follow.\\\",\\n      \\\"facts\\\": [],\\n      \\\"expected_answer\\\": \\\"Thank you for your feedback. We appreciate you sharing your thoughts.\\\"\\n    }\\n  ]\\n}\",\"2\":null,\"3\":\"{\\n  \\\"items\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"category\\\": \\\"Specific Query\\\",\\n      \\\"query_text\\\": \\\"Can you explain how I can book a test drive and what details I need to provide for the request?\\\",\\n      \\\"facts\\\": [\\n        \\\"Welcome to Aventro Motors Pvt. Ltd.!  Experience the future of mobility from the comfort of your home. Book a test drive for any Aventro car, and we\\u2019ll bring your chosen model to your doorstep, anywhere in India.\\\",\\n        \\\"Fill in the form below or contac