he physical key into the keyhole.\\\",\\n        \\\"Turn the key (usually clockwise) to unlock the door manually.\\\"\\n      ],\\n      \\\"expected_answer\\\": \\\"To unlock your Aventro Motors car when the remote battery is dead, first locate the hidden physical key by pressing the release button on your remote, then find the key slot on your car (it may be exposed near the driver's door handle or hidden under a cover), insert the key into the keyhole, and turn it clockwise to unlock the door.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"category\\\": \\\"Compound Query\\\",\\n      \\\"query_text\\\": \\\"Can you explain the step-by-step process to open my Aventro Motors car door when my remote battery is dead, and also tell me if the car alarm might go off during the process?\\\",\\n      \\\"facts\\\": [\\n        \\\"If your Aventro Motors car key remote battery is dead and you're unable to unlock your car using the remote, you can still access your vehicle using the physical key. Follow these simple steps:\\\",\\n        \\\"Most Aventro car key fobs have a hidden physical key.\\\",\\n        \\\"Look for a release button or switch on your remote.\\\",\\n        \\\"Some models: The physical key slot is exposed and visible near the driver's door handle.\\\",\\n        \\\"Other models: The key slot might be hidden under a cover on the door handle. Look for a small indent or slot. Gently pry off the cover (if applicable) using the physical key or your fingernail.\\\",\\n        \\\"Insert the physical key into the keyhole.\\\",\\n        \\\"Turn the key (usually clockwise) to unlock the door manually.\\\",\\n        \\\"Alarm: Some cars may trigger the alarm when opened manually. Don\\u2019t worry\\u2014once inside, place the key fob near the start\\/ignition button (if using push start) or insert it into the ignition to recognize the key and disarm the alarm.\\\"\\n      ],\\n      \\\"expected_answer\\\": \\\"To open your Aventro Motors car door when the remote battery is dead, first locate the hidden physical key by using the release button on your remote, then find the key slot (which could be exposed or hidden under a cover), insert the key into the keyhole, and turn it clockwise to unlock. Additionally, while some cars may trigger the alarm when opened manually, simply place the key fob near the start button or insert it into the ignition once inside to disarm the alarm.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"category\\\": \\\"Instructional Query\\\",\\n      \\\"query_text\\\": \\\"I need step-by-step guidance on how to use my physical key to open my Aventro Motors car when the remote battery dies. Can you help?\\\",\\n      \\\"facts\\\": [\\n        \\\"If your Aventro Motors car key remote battery is dead and you're unable to unlock your car using the remote, you can still access your vehicle using the physical key. Follow these simple steps:\\\",\\n        \\\"Most Aventro car key fobs have a hidden physical key.\\\",\\n        \\\"Look for a release button or switch on your remote.\\\",\\n        \\\"Some models: The physical key slot is exposed and visible near the driver's door handle.\\\",\\n        \\\"Other models: The key slot might be hidden under a cover on the door handle. Look for a small indent or slot. Gently pry off the cover (if applicable) using the physical key or your fingernail.\\\",\\n        \\\"Insert the physical key into the keyhole.\\\",\\n        \\\"Turn the key (usually clockwise) to unlock the door manually.\\\",\\n        \\\"Replace Remote Battery: As soon as possible, replace the battery in your key remote to restore full functionality.\\\"\\n      ],\\n      \\\"expected_answer\\\": \\\"To use your physical key when the Aventro Motors remote battery dies: first, locate the hidden physical key by pressing the release button on your remote; next, find the key slot on your car, which may be visible near the driver's door handle or hidden under a cover; then, insert the physical key into the keyhole and turn it clockwise to unlock the door; finally, replace the remote battery as soon as possible to restore full functionality.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"category\\\": \\\"Opinion-Based Query\\\",\\n      \\\"query_text\\\": \\\"In your opinion, is it better to use the physical key regularly or replace the remote battery quickly to avoid manual unlocking?\\\",\\n      \\\"facts\\\": [\\n        \\\"Replace Remote Battery: As soon as possible, replace the battery in your key remote to restore full functionality.\\\"\\n      ],\\n      \\\"expected_answer\\\": \\\"It is recommended to replace the remote battery as soon as possible to restore full functionality.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"category\\\": \\\"Error\\/Issue Query\\\",\\n      \\\"query_text\\\": \\\"I followed the steps to use the physical key, but my Aventro Motors car still isn't unlocking. What might be wrong?\\\",\\n      \\\"facts\\\": [\\n        \\\"If your Aventro Motors car key remote battery is dead and you're unable to unlock your car using the remote, you can still access your vehicle using the physical key. Follow these simple steps:\\\",\\n        \\\"Most Aventro car key fobs have a hidden physical key.\\\",\\n        \\\"Look for a release button or switch on your remote.\\\",\\n        \\\"Some models: The physical key slot is exposed and visible near the driver's door handle.\\\",\\n        \\\"Other models: The key slot might be hidden under a cover on the door handle. Look for a small indent or slot. Gently pry off the cover (if applicable) using the physical key or your fingernail.\\\",\\n        \\\"Insert the physical key into the keyhole.\\\",\\n        \\\"Turn the key (usually clockwise) to unlock the door manually.\\\"\\n      ],\\n      \\\"expected_answer\\\": \\\"Please ensure that you have correctly located the hidden physical key and are using the appropriate key slot (which could be visible or hidden under a cover). Also, make sure to insert the key proper